body: "## Observed failure\nThe scheduled GitHub issue sync on current main `0bb9d6ed9956886de5df2f987b5f5640e38ea518`, using `pm-github@2026.10.29`, exits 1 at the ownership preflight:\n\n> GitHub issue #5 has multiple existing owners; import plan is not idempotent. No item was written for this issue. No branch was published.\n\n[Hosted run and failing job](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rlm/actions/runs/41297675184/job/124821865302). This is a repository tracker-data collision, not a demonstrated RLM inference/runtime defect. The fail-closed guard is working and should remain.\n\n## Exact competing records\nBoth records are closed, but both declare ownership of [issue #5](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rlm/issues/5):\n- [pm-rlm-sr0b](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rlm/blob/0bb9d6ed9956886de5df2f987b5f5640e38ea518/.agents/pm/issues/pm-rlm-sr0b.toon): description begins `GitHub issue https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rlm/issues/5.`; this is an ownership declaration, not an incidental prose mention. It retains implementation evidence and regression references.\n- [pm-rlm-github-dfe63798395a-5](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rlm/blob/0bb9d6ed9956886de5df2f987b5f5640e38ea518/.agents/pm/issues/pm-rlm-github-dfe63798395a-5.toon): exact `gh:unbraind/pm-rlm#5` tag plus `github_url`, `github_number: 5` and imported provider metadata.\n\nThe pinned [identity contract](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/blob/da0366ac6e81f35ce66bcfe5efb3b386a1c3fd84/docs/identity-collisions.md) explicitly recognizes leading declarations and structured provenance as claims. Its narrow tag-only repair is not suitable for two independently declared owners; manually reviewed ownership reconciliation is required.\n\n## Expected outcome and impact\nOne unambiguous import owner for each GitHub identity, while both historical records, their content, delivery evidence, relationships and append-only histories remain recoverable. The current collision blocks the scheduled tracker refresh; no data loss or published-branch mutation is established by this observation.\n\n## Reproduction / limits\nInspect the two records on the immutable commit above and the referenced hosted sync log. A read-only identity diagnosis can further show their claims. No local provider import, repair mutation, model call or full RLM suite was executed in this review. The workflow-version-only merge exposed this failure, but this report does not claim it created the older duplicate records.\n\n## Acceptance / regression criteria\n- Independently select the canonical provider owner and represent the other record as a durable related implementation record without a second ownership declaration. Do not delete either record or its history to silence the guard.\n- Back up and verify recoverability before the audited repair; preserve original IDs, content, relationships, completion/release provenance and existing history bytes.\n- Diagnose the complete all-status tracker, including any further collisions, rather than fixing only the first reported identity.\n- Verify one import owner for #5, an initial complete sync and a repeated idempotent sync, with no unrelated item changes and no new duplicates.\n- Retain fail-closed ambiguity, scoped commit and privacy gates, and record exact revision/commands/results.\n\n## Dedup\nChecked all 48 existing all-status issues/PRs, their available conversation comments and all 36 current canonical PM records. #5 is the delivered runtime validation fix, not this sync ownership repair. No dedicated existing repair owner was found."
